# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The CSP ships as Report-Only on purpose. This site loads third-party
# embeds (YouTube, Google Maps) and posts forms to FormSubmit, and carries an inline
# JSON-LD block, and a policy that is merely *close* to correct fails silently:
# the browser drops the resource with no visible error in the page. Read the
# reports from the deployed URL — not localhost, which proves nothing about
# what the edge actually serves — then promote to `Content-Security-Policy`.
#
# Before promoting, two things must be settled:
#
#   * `script-src` gates <script> elements of every type, including
#     `application/ld+json`. Enforcing this policy as written would drop the
#     structured data in index.html and cost the church its rich results. Add
#     that block's sha256 to `script-src` first. (/theme-init.js is a real
#     file, so 'self' already covers it.)
#   * Add `upgrade-insecure-requests` back. It is omitted below because the
#     spec says it is ignored in a report-only policy, and Chrome logs an
#     error saying so — twice on every page load, for every visitor, drowning
#     out the reports this policy exists to collect.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-src https://www.google.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'

# Vite fingerprints everything in /assets, so the filename changes whenever the
# content does. These can be cached forever.
# Browsers may keep them forever, but Cloudflare's shared cache must not: during a
# deploy an asset request can briefly fall through to the SPA fallback, and a
# year-long edge cache would then serve index.html as the JS bundle to everyone
# on that edge.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Cloudflare-CDN-Cache-Control: no-store

# Images keep their names across deploys, so they get a day rather than a year.
/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
# head-boot.js keeps its name across deploys: short cache, never immutable.
/head-boot.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
